🚽 Test case: #196 -- same struct-tag check as
🚽 struct_pointer_tag_mismatch_decl_fail.brainrot, but for a FUNCTION CALL
🚽 argument bound to a pointer-to-struct parameter (PR #248 review, round
🚽 2, finding 1's call-argument reproduction). Without this check,
🚽 enter_function_scope() (ast.c) would follow `&r`'s address using
🚽 `bump`'s declared `gang Point *pp` layout on an actually Rect-shaped
🚽 blob.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
    rizz h;
};

skibidi bump(gang Point *pp) {
    pp.x = 99;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Rect r;
    r.w = 11;
    bump(&r);
    yapping("%d", r.w);
}
